WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:12.520
42. The Large Hadron Collider. In Switzerland, in a huge tunnel deep underground, is a giant

2
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:18.720
scientific instrument. It's called the Large Hadron Collider, LHC. It was built with the

3
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:24.880
help of more than 10,000 scientists from over 100 different countries to help people learn

4
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:31.920
more about how our world began. The LHC was built to make different particles collide,

5
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:39.280
crash into each other, at extremely high speeds. The LHC is so big, 17 miles long,

6
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.840
to allow the particles to build up as much speed as possible. The particles this machine

7
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:52.080
uses are called hadrons. They're even smaller than atoms. Scientists believe that by smashing

8
00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:58.200
them into each other at high speeds, we can learn more about the Big Bang. The Big Bang

9
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.760
is the name of a theory about how the Earth was formed. The theory guesses that our part

10
00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:10.680
of the universe used to be only a few centimeters of hot space. Then, for some reason, this

11
00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:19.640
space began to expand and cool until it eventually became the vast, cold universe we now have.

12
00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:26.600
Scientists want to know why. The LHC tries to recreate the Big Bang. It spins hadrons

13
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:31.840
until they are moving at almost the speed of light. The great speed makes them very

14
00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:38.680
hot like they would have been before the Big Bang. Then, when they collide, they produce

15
00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:45.280
a soup of other particles. Scientists are very curious about these other particles.

16
00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.920
They believe that studying the beginning of the universe can help them understand how

17
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:56.640
the universe works now. The LHC will also help scientists try to answer other questions

18
00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:03.600
like what is most of the universe made of and what makes some things have weight. We

19
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:09.520
don't know if the LHC will actually provide answers, but for now, it's as close as we

20
00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:10.320
can get.
